stagingTools.description:
Use this MCP to deploy, manage, and debug applications on Railway. Call the direct tools for reads and routine operations — listing projects/services/variables/domains, inspecting config, status, logs, metrics, setting variables, updating service settings, creating services, and searching the Railway docs. Reach for the `railway-agent` tool when a task is genuinely complex or open-ended (multi-service debugging, incident investigation, operations that span many steps or need Railway-side reasoning). Fall back to the local Railway CLI when needed. Confirm with the user before destructive actions (e.g. `accept-deploy`).

Create a new service in a project from a Docker image, or an empty service to configure later (e.g. before setting variables and attaching a source). Public images only: credentials for a private registry are not accepted here — the user sets them on the service in the Railway dashboard. Pass staged: true to stage the service in one environment instead of applying it live — it then only becomes real when the staged changes are committed with accept-deploy. To create a service from a GitHub repository, use create-deployment instead.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__railway__create_service(args: {
  // Environment ID to create the service in. If omitted, the service is created in all non-fork environments. Required when staged is true.
  environmentId?: string;
  // Docker image to deploy, e.g. 'redis' or 'ghcr.io/org/app:latest'. Omit to create an empty service.
  image?: string;
  // Name for the new service. If omitted, a name is derived from the image or generated.
  name?: string;
  // The project ID to create the service in
  projectId: string;
  // Stage the service in the environment's pending changes instead of applying it live. The service shows up on the canvas immediately but gets no instance until accept-deploy commits the staged changes (or the user applies them in the dashboard). Requires environmentId.
  staged?: boolean;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  environment: { id: string | null; scope: "specific" | "all_non_fork"; };
  project: { id: string; name: string; };
  service: { id: string; name: string; };
  // Docker image source, or null for an empty service
  source: { image: string; } | null;
  // Present when the service was staged instead of applied. The service exists but has no instance until the staged changes are committed with accept-deploy.
  staged: {
  // Total changes now staged in the environment
  changeCount: number;
  // The environment patch holding the change
  patchId: string;
} | null;
}>>; };
```

Use this MCP to deploy, manage, and debug applications on Railway. Call the direct tools for reads and routine operations — listing projects/services/variables/domains, inspecting config, status, logs, metrics, setting variables, updating service settings, creating services, and searching the Railway docs. Reach for the `railway-agent` tool when a task is genuinely complex or open-ended (multi-service debugging, incident investigation, operations that span many steps or need Railway-side reasoning). Fall back to the local Railway CLI when needed. Confirm with the user before destructive actions (e.g. `accept-deploy`).

Update a service's configuration: build/start/pre-deploy commands and pre-deploy timeout, builder, healthcheck, sleep mode, root directory, cron schedule, Dockerfile path, restart policy, config file path, watch patterns, replicas per region, resource limits, deployment overlap/draining, outbound IPv6, and the private network endpoint name. Only the fields you pass are changed. Config changes apply on the service's next deployment (use redeploy to apply immediately); regions and limits scale the running deployment right away, and privateNetworkEndpoint is committed to the environment and redeploys the service. Pass staged: true to stage the update in one environment's pending changes instead of writing it to the service — it then applies when the staged changes are committed with accept-deploy. Source changes are not handled by this tool (use connect-service-source), and private registry credentials are set by the user in the Railway dashboard.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__railway__update_service(args: {
  // Custom build command
  buildCommand?: string;
  // Build system for services without a Dockerfile. RAILPACK is the default; NIXPACKS is the legacy builder.
  builder?: "RAILPACK" | "NIXPACKS";
  // Cron schedule, e.g. '0 * * * *'. Minimum interval is 5 minutes. Pass null to remove the schedule and run the service continuously.
  cronSchedule?: string | null;
  // Path to a custom Dockerfile
  dockerfilePath?: string;
  // Seconds between the old deployment's containers receiving SIGTERM and SIGKILL. Pass null to reset to the default.
  drainingSeconds?: number | null;
  // Environment to update. If omitted, the service is updated in all environments. Required when staged is true.
  environmentId?: string;
  // HTTP healthcheck path, e.g. /health
  healthcheckPath?: string;
  // Healthcheck timeout in seconds (0-3600). Pass null to reset.
  healthcheckTimeout?: number | null;
  // Enable/disable outbound IPv6 internet access
  ipv6EgressEnabled?: boolean;
  // Resource limits per replica, capped by the workspace plan. Only the values you pass change.
  limits?: { memoryGB?: number; vCPUs?: number; };
  // Seconds the old deployment keeps serving after the new one is healthy. Pass null to reset to the default.
  overlapSeconds?: number | null;
  // Commands run before each deploy
  preDeployCommand?: Array<string>;
  // How long the pre-deploy command may run, in seconds (1-3600). Pass null to reset to the default.
  preDeployTimeoutSeconds?: number | null;
  // The service's private DNS label, reachable as <label>.railway.internal: lowercase letters, digits and hyphens.
  privateNetworkEndpoint?: string;
  // The project ID
  projectId: string;
  // Path to a railway config file, e.g. railway.toml
  railwayConfigFile?: string;
  // Replicas per region, e.g. { "us-west2": { "numReplicas": 2 } }. Replaces the whole region map: a region absent from it is removed. Services with a volume run in one region only.
  regions?: { [key: string]: { numReplicas: number; }; };
  // Max restart retries for ON_FAILURE policy
  restartPolicyMaxRetries?: number;
  // Restart policy for crashed deployments
  restartPolicyType?: "ALWAYS" | "NEVER" | "ON_FAILURE";
  // Root directory for builds, e.g. /packages/api. With staged: true this counts as a source change: committing it recreates the service's deployment triggers and re-resolves its GitHub authorization from whoever commits. Stage it on its own if that matters.
  rootDirectory?: string;
  // The service ID
  serviceId: string;
  // Enable/disable app sleeping (serverless mode)
  sleepApplication?: boolean;
  // Stage the change in the environment's pending changes instead of applying it live. It takes effect only when the staged changes are committed with accept-deploy (or the user applies them in the dashboard).
  staged?: boolean;
  // Custom start command
  startCommand?: string;
  // File patterns that trigger automatic redeploys
  watchPatterns?: Array<string>;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  // Environment updated, or null when all environments were
  environmentId: string | null;
  service: { id: string; name: string; };
  // Present when the change was staged instead of applied. It takes effect only when the staged changes are committed with accept-deploy.
  staged: {
  // Total changes now staged in the environment
  changeCount: number;
  // The environment patch holding the change
  patchId: string;
} | null;
  updatedFields: Array<string>;
}>>; };
```

Use this MCP to deploy, manage, and debug applications on Railway. Call the direct tools for reads and routine operations — listing projects/services/variables/domains, inspecting config, status, logs, metrics, setting variables, updating service settings, creating services, and searching the Railway docs. Reach for the `railway-agent` tool when a task is genuinely complex or open-ended (multi-service debugging, incident investigation, operations that span many steps or need Railway-side reasoning). Fall back to the local Railway CLI when needed. Confirm with the user before destructive actions (e.g. `accept-deploy`).

Show the changes staged in a Railway environment that accept-deploy would commit: per resource (service, volume, bucket, group) the action — create, delete, update — and each changed field with its live and staged value. Variable values and registry credentials are redacted to names. Also reports whether the patch is destructive and whether a commit is already applying. Review this before calling accept-deploy. If environmentId is omitted, the production environment is used.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__railway__get_staged_changes(args: {
  // Environment to inspect. Defaults to `production` if present, otherwise the project's oldest environment.
  environmentId?: string;
  // The project ID
  projectId: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  // True when committing would delete a service, volume or bucket, or otherwise destroy data. accept-deploy may refuse such commits; the user can apply them from the dashboard.
  destructive: boolean;
  environment: { id: string; name: string; };
  // Staged private-networking toggle, if any
  privateNetworkDisabled: {
  destructive: boolean;
  displayName: string;
  // Live value as displayed; empty when added
  from: string;
  // Config path, e.g. services.<id>.deploy.startCommand
  path: string;
  // Staged value as displayed; empty when removed
  to: string;
  type: "added" | "removed" | "updated";
} | null;
  project: { id: string; name: string; };
  // Staged changes grouped by the service, volume, bucket or group they touch
  resources: Array<{ action: "create" | "delete" | "update"; changes: Array<{
  destructive: boolean;
  displayName: string;
  // Live value as displayed; empty when added
  from: string;
  // Config path, e.g. services.<id>.deploy.startCommand
  path: string;
  // Staged value as displayed; empty when removed
  to: string;
  type: "added" | "removed" | "updated";
}>; id: string; kind: "service" | "volume" | "bucket" | "group"; name: string; }>;
  // Staged shared-variable changes, names only
  sharedVariables: Array<{
  destructive: boolean;
  displayName: string;
  // Live value as displayed; empty when added
  from: string;
  // Config path, e.g. services.<id>.deploy.startCommand
  path: string;
  // Staged value as displayed; empty when removed
  to: string;
  type: "added" | "removed" | "updated";
}>;
  // The environment's pending patch, or null when nothing is staged
  staged: {
  changeCount: number;
  createdAt: string;
  message: string | null;
  patchId: string;
  // STAGED: pending, commit with accept-deploy. APPLYING: a commit is in progress; wait for it to settle before staging more.
  status: "STAGED" | "APPLYING";
  updatedAt: string;
} | null;
}>>; };
```
